@startuml workflow-feature
' The feature lane: from a spoken idea to a spec live in production.
'
' One of three lane diagrams (feature, work package, fix). The branches
' each step works on are in docs/development/branching-model.puml.
' The pre-commit hook renders the PNG for any staged .puml automatically;
' render the PDF with `plantuml -tpdf docs/development/workflow-feature.puml`.
'
' Scope: the route work takes, not every skill. A skill that runs inside
' another step (tpl-po-check inside promotion, tpl-session-name inside specify
' and merge, tpl-prepare-docs-reference inside the merge) is named on the
' step that calls it.

title The feature lane

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam ArrowFontColor #666666

skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #999999
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  FontSize 12
  roundCorner 8
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #BBBBBB
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  FontColor #777777
  FontSize 11
  FontStyle plain
}

package "Capture" {
  rectangle "**Voice planning session**\non claude.ai, usually mobile" as session #FFF8F0
  rectangle "**Session brief**\ndocs/sessions/YYYY-MM-DD-topic.md" as brief
  rectangle "**tpl-review-session-notes**\ncreates what the brief declares" as notes #F0F6FF
}

package "Backlog" {
  rectangle "**Backlog capture**\ndocs/features/backlog/ft-*.md\nunnumbered, no committed phase" as capture
  rectangle "**tpl-review-backlog**\nthe ceremony: what enters a phase" as ceremony #F0F6FF
  rectangle "**tpl-split-feature**\nright-sizes an oversized capture\ninto ordered, shippable slices" as split #F0F6FF
}

package "Promotion  (on main)" {
  rectangle "**tpl-promote-backlog-spec**\nallocates the number; asks the\nproduct owner first; writes\n**Target branch** into the spec" as promote #F0F6FF
  rectangle "**feature/NNN-slug**\ncut from main and pushed" as featbranch #F0F6FF
}

package "Build  (task branches into feature/NNN-slug)" {
  rectangle "**/speckit.specify**\nrun from the feature branch;\nits hook cuts the first task branch" as specify #F0FFF4
  rectangle "**/speckit.clarify**  every NEEDS CLARIFICATION resolved\n**/speckit.plan**  stack, data model, ER diagram;\noperator review before any migration\n**/speckit.tasks**  dependency-ordered tasks.md\n**/speckit.analyze**  contradictions found" as middle #F0FFF4
  rectangle "**/speckit.implement**\nTDD, one user story at a time,\neach on its own task branch" as implement #F0FFF4
  rectangle "**/speckit.checklist**\nthen **/speckit.converge**\nappends whatever is unbuilt" as converge #F0FFF4
  rectangle "**tpl-merge**, task merge\nchecks (task tier) green,\npest on the operator's say so;\nsync onto the feature branch" as taskmerge #F0F6FF
}

package "Release" {
  rectangle "**tpl-merge**, feature merge\nmain merged in, full checks,\npest mandatory, migration order,\nreview and conformance gates" as featmerge #F0F6FF
  rectangle "**/code-review**\nThe operator triggers it.\nNever launched by a skill." as review #FFF0F0
  rectangle "**main**\nindexes and roadmap regenerated\nin a docs-only follow-up PR" as main
  rectangle "**release-please PR**\nmerging it publishes the\nrelease and fires the deploy" as release
  rectangle "**Live**" as live #F0FFF0
  rectangle "**tpl-archive-spec**\nin the feature merge's PR,\nwhen the spec is finished" as archive #F0F6FF
}

session --> brief : dictated, then\nasked for as a brief
brief --> notes
notes --> capture : feature intent
capture --> ceremony
ceremony --> split : oversized
ceremony --> promote : right-sized
split --> promote : slice by slice
promote --> featbranch
featbranch --> specify
specify --> middle
middle --> implement
implement --> converge
converge --> implement : unbuilt work found
implement --> taskmerge : each task branch
middle --> taskmerge : the document phases
taskmerge --> featbranch : squash into\nthe feature branch
converge --> featmerge : nothing left unbuilt
review ..> featmerge : outstanding gate
archive ..> featmerge
featmerge --> main
main --> release
release --> live

note bottom of featbranch
  One feature branch per spec.
  A slice of a split capture is
  its own spec, so its own branch.
end note

@enduml
